{
 "id": "E12",
 "title": "Pro presses as a matter of course: its opponents hunt the carrier from 16 m and lift a stick again after a second",
 "date": "2026-11-25",
 "pillar": "P6 a level is harder by better play; the owner's ladder is an aggression ladder (R-0041: \"rookie bots rarely check, pro check as a matter of course, all-star hunt the carrier\")",
 "targets": [
  "T8"
 ],
 "hypothesis": "The regular planning hand wins 88 % at pro on hockey.thirdlife (thirdjam: 78 % for the same hand; the Director's band is 60-80 %). E10 showed that all-star's finishing does not make pro harder. What separates the levels in thirdjam's own table, apart from legs, is how they press: the distance from which the bots leave their shape to go at the carrier (hunt_radius_m: pro 11 m, all-star 30) and how soon a bot may lift a stick again (lift_cooldown_frames: rookie 150 since E09, pro 90, all-star 45). The change, pro only: hunt from 16 m, lift again after 60 frames. The kept rules make this pressure fair where thirdjam's was not: a hit on your first touch only staggers you (E07), a knockdown lasts a second (E04), and nobody takes the puck without a key (E03). Expected: the regular planning hand at pro back inside 60-80 %; the novice and the good still apart from it; more hits thrown at the human and his seconds on the ice up a little (T6 is the price to watch: at most 5 s).",
